Lemon Blueberry Melomel (Makes One Gallon)

Modified from: reddit.com/r/mead/comments/zn2gup/blueberry_lemon_mead/

MeadTools Estimates:
OG: 1.084
FG: 0.996
ABV: 10.6%

Ingredients:

Primary:
- 1 Gallon Water
- 3 Pounds Wildflower Honey
- 1/2 Packet of S-04

Secondary:
- 1 Can Great Value Blueberry Pie Filling
- Zest of 2-3 Lemons

Procedure:

1. Add water and honey to 2 gallon fermenting bucket. Stir until combined and aerated.
2. Pitch yeast. Store in a cool, dry place until airlock shows less than 1 bubble per minute.
3. Add muslin bag containing pie filling and lemon zest to a 1 gallon carboy.
4. Rack over from bucket. Store in secondary for 3 weeks, or until bubbling has stopped.
5. Rack into bottles. Age 6 months.
